From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc2145: do not fail volatile control reads while
 suspended

gc2145_g_volatile_ctrl() returns -EIO when the sensor is runtime suspended,
which is its normal state before anything streams. Any client that reads
controls while enumerating therefore gets an error. libcamera does exactly
that, on every single start:

  ERROR V4L2 v4l2_device.cpp:272 'gc2145 3-003c':
        Unable to read control 0x00980911: Input/output error

0x00980911 is V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE. It is volatile because

  v4l2_ctrl_auto_cluster(3, &ctrls->auto_exposure, V4L2_EXPOSURE_MANUAL, true);

marks the cluster's slaves volatile, so reading it lands here even though the
switch below only handles the cluster masters.

Report success and leave the cached value instead. This is what
gc2145_s_ctrl() already does for the same condition a hundred lines below -

  if (!pm_runtime_get_if_in_use(&sensor->i2c_client->dev))
          return 0;

- deferring to the setup done when streaming starts. There is no value to
read back from a powered-down sensor, and the cached one is the honest
answer; -EIO says the hardware failed, which it did not.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -1492,8 +1492,22 @@
 
 	/* v4l2_ctrl_lock() locks our own mutex */
 
+	/*
+	 * There is nothing to read back while the sensor is suspended, and
+	 * that is the normal state before streaming starts. Keep the cached
+	 * value and report success, the way gc2145_s_ctrl() already defers
+	 * writes until the stream-start handler setup applies them. Failing
+	 * here instead breaks every client that reads controls while
+	 * enumerating - libcamera does, and logs
+	 *
+	 *   'gc2145 3-003c': Unable to read control 0x00980911:
+	 *   Input/output error
+	 *
+	 * for V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE, which is volatile because it is a slave of
+	 * the auto exposure cluster.
+	 */
 	if (!pm_runtime_get_if_in_use(dev))
-		return -EIO;
+		return 0;
 
 	switch (ctrl->id) {
 	case V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE_AUTO:
